.TH geectl-remote-create-package 1  "geectl-remote-create-package 0.2.3" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-remote\-create\-package \- Create a package. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the creation. Without `\-\-scmsync` and `\-\-force` the package is created directly; with either, the creation goes through the options form, which refuses an existing package unless `\-\-force` is set and refuses a project managed in git
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl remote create\-package\fR [\fB\-\-scmsync\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-title\fR> <\fB\-\-description\fR> <\fIPROJECT\fR> <\fIPACKAGE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a package. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the creation. Without `\-\-scmsync` and `\-\-force` the package is created directly; with either, the creation goes through the options form, which refuses an existing package unless `\-\-force` is set and refuses a project managed in git
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-title\fR \fI<TITLE>\fR
The package title
.TP
\fB\-\-description\fR \fI<DESCRIPTION>\fR
The package description
.TP
\fB\-\-scmsync\fR \fI<SCMSYNC>\fR
The git repository and branch the package syncs its sources from, as `url#branch`
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite the package when it already exists
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project to create the package in
.TP
<\fIPACKAGE\fR>
The package to create
.SH VERSION
v0.2.3
